    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **288 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp19Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller that handles `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Dedicated `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 added a `static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` field, matching the logger name the acceptance infrastructure (`AuditLogCapture`) captures.\n\n2. **Log line on success** \u2014 right after `saveOwner(owner)` in `addOwner`, it logs the authenticated user, the new owner's id, and membership number:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created: user={} ownerId={} membershipNumber={}\",\n       currentUsername(), owner.getId(), owner.getMembershipNumber());\n   ```\n   This is placed after the persist call so the generated `id` is populated, and only after all rejection paths (conflict/quota checks) have passed \u2014 so it logs only genuinely successful creations.\n\n3. **Authenticated user resolution** \u2014 a `currentUsername()` helper reads the name from `SecurityContextHolder`, falling back to `\"anonymous\"` if unauthenticated.\n\nThe observed log output confirms the behavior: `AUDIT - owner created: user=acceptance-admin ownerId=11 membershipNumber=11`.",
